  {t: "Old", b: "Song of Solomon", c: "General Knowledge", d: "Hard", q: "According to tradition, Song of Solomon was written when Solomon was young and in love. What later book attributes wisdom to him in old age?", a: "Ecclesiastes", w: ["Proverbs", "1 Kings", "2 Chronicles"]},
  {t: "Old", b: "Song of Solomon", c: "People", d: "Hard", q: "In Song of Solomon 5:15, the beloved's legs are compared to what?", a: "Pillars of marble set on bases of gold", w: ["Strong oak trunks", "The legs of a deer", "Bronze columns"]},
  {t: "Old", b: "Song of Solomon", c: "General Knowledge", d: "Hard", q: "Song of Solomon's imagery of the beloved as a shepherd has been connected to which New Testament passage?", a: "Jesus as the Good Shepherd in John 10", w: ["Paul as a shepherd in Acts 20", "Peter as a shepherd in 1 Peter 5", "David as a shepherd in Acts 13"]},
  {t: "Old", b: "Song of Solomon", c: "Prophecy", d: "Hard", q: "The 'garden enclosed' of Song of Solomon 4:12 is interpreted by Eastern Orthodox tradition as representing:", a: "The Theotokos (Virgin Mary)", w: ["The Holy Sepulchre", "The Ark of the Covenant", "The city of Jerusalem"]},
  {t: "Old", b: "Song of Solomon", c: "Events", d: "Medium", q: "What does the bride say the daughters of Jerusalem should tell Solomon if she is found in Song of Solomon 5:8?", a: "That she is sick with love", w: ["That she is lost", "That she is in danger", "That she has returned home"]},
  {t: "Old", b: "Song of Solomon", c: "People", d: "Hard", q: "The bride describes her beloved's hands in Song of Solomon 5:14 as being set with what?", a: "Beryl or topaz", w: ["Rubies", "Sapphires", "Diamonds"]},
  {t: "Old", b: "Song of Solomon", c: "Events", d: "Hard", q: "What does the bride say the watchmen do to her in Song of Solomon 5:7?", a: "They took away her veil from her", w: ["They helped her find her beloved", "They gave her food and shelter", "They told her to go home"]},
  {t: "Old", b: "Song of Solomon", c: "General Knowledge", d: "Hard", q: "Song of Solomon is unique among biblical books because:", a: "It contains no mention of God, law, or sin", w: ["It is the shortest book", "It is written in Aramaic", "It has no poetry"]},
  {t: "Old", b: "Song of Solomon", c: "Events", d: "Hard", q: "What does the bride say in Song of Solomon 8:14 about the mountains?", a: "Let my beloved come to his garden and eat its choicest fruits", w: ["Let us flee to the mountains", "The mountains will tremble", "The mountains will bring peace"]},
  {t: "Old", b: "Song of Solomon", c: "Numbers", d: "Hard", q: "The bride describes 'three hundred' warriors surrounding Solomon in which verse?", a: "Song of Solomon 3:7 — sixty mighty men", w: ["Song of Solomon 2:4", "Song of Solomon 5:10", "Song of Solomon 8:6"]},
  {t: "Old", b: "Song of Solomon", c: "People", d: "Hard", q: "What does the bride say about her beloved's voice in Song of Solomon 2:8 and 5:2?", a: "She recognizes it and it causes her heart to thrill", w: ["She has never heard it", "It is frightening", "It is soft and weak"]},
  {t: "Old", b: "Song of Solomon", c: "Prophecy", d: "Hard", q: "The refrain about not awakening love until it pleases (Song of Solomon 2:7) has been interpreted as meaning:", a: "True love cannot be forced or rushed", w: ["Love is forbidden", "Love is only for the elderly", "Love is a test from God"]},
  {t: "Old", b: "Song of Solomon", c: "General Knowledge", d: "Hard", q: "In Song of Solomon 8:6, love is described as being set as a seal. A seal in the ancient world signified:", a: "Ownership and authority", w: ["Secrecy", "Punishment", "Mourning"]},
  {t: "Old", b: "Song of Solomon", c: "People", d: "Hard", q: "In Song of Solomon 6:9, the bride is compared to whom as 'the perfect one'?", a: "The only daughter of her mother", w: ["The queen of Sheba", "The daughter of Pharaoh", "The wife of Boaz"]},
  {t: "Old", b: "Song of Solomon", c: "Events", d: "Hard", q: "What does the bride say in Song of Solomon 4:16 that the winds should do?", a: "Blow upon her garden so its spices may flow out", w: ["Blow away the enemies", "Carry her to the king", "Bring the cool of evening"]},
  {t: "Old", b: "Song of Solomon", c: "General Knowledge", d: "Hard", q: "According to some traditions, Song of Solomon was written to celebrate the marriage of Solomon to which foreign queen?", a: "The daughter of Pharaoh", w: ["The queen of Sheba", "Esther", "Jezebel"]},
  {t: "Old", b: "Song of Solomon", c: "People", d: "Hard", q: "What does the bride say about her beloved's temples in Song of Solomon 5:13?", a: "They are like beds of spices", w: ["They are scarlet", "They are like the sun", "They are like burnished gold"]},
  {t: "Old", b: "Song of Solomon", c: "Numbers", d: "Hard", q: "How many mighty men does Solomon have surrounding his bed in Song of Solomon 3:7?", a: "Sixty", w: ["Thirty", "Forty", "Eighty"]},
  {t: "Old", b: "Song of Solomon", c: "General Knowledge", d: "Hard", q: "The Song of Solomon is read during the Jewish feast of Passover because:", a: "The love it describes is seen as God's love for Israel at the Exodus", w: ["It mentions the lamb", "It discusses sacrifice", "It was written during the Exodus"]},
  {t: "Old", b: "Song of Solomon", c: "Prophecy", d: "Hard", q: "In Christian tradition, Song of Solomon 2:1 ('I am the rose of Sharon') is applied to:", a: "Christ or the Church", w: ["The Virgin Mary alone", "The Old Testament prophets", "The twelve tribes"]},
  {t: "Old", b: "Song of Solomon", c: "General Knowledge", d: "Hard", q: "Which of the early Church Fathers wrote a lengthy commentary on Song of Solomon interpreting it allegorically?", a: "Origen of Alexandria", w: ["Augustine of Hippo", "Tertullian", "Clement of Rome"]},
  {t: "Old", b: "Song of Solomon", c: "General Knowledge", d: "Hard", q: "The Song of Solomon is the only book of the Bible where the word 'love' appears more frequently than in which book?", a: "It uses 'love' or 'beloved' more than any other book per chapter", w: ["Psalms", "Proverbs", "1 Corinthians"]},
  {t: "Old", b: "Song of Solomon", c: "People", d: "Hard", q: "The bride's description of her beloved in Song of Solomon 5:10-16 is the only extended physical description of whom in the entire Bible?", a: "Solomon", w: ["David", "Jesus", "Moses"]},
  {t: "Old", b: "Song of Solomon", c: "Events", d: "Hard", q: "What does the bride compare love to in Song of Solomon 8:7?", a: "A fire that cannot be quenched by many waters", w: ["A flood that covers the earth", "A wind that cannot be held", "A stone that cannot be moved"]}
